  "body": "The previous minimal SDK lacked the activity API required by the cache adapter. This builds a separate pinned GLX/X11/noPython libpandagl with the unchanged activity/runtime included once, plus separately compiled C cache and C++ adapter objects. All 33 required APIs are defined in that image; strict -Wl,-z,defs rejects missing activity. The original read tail is retained. Actual runtime installation and identity attachment remain later gates.\n\nFinal HEAD: 45df9244b4e212af3c5f18628ba7639608a0b4cd. Verifier implementation: faeadbbc6537826dfdb4bb3bea6132fc6a7e2fa7; actual SDK build implementation: 326171e5d23e69344462360c3d4da464ad562a87. Base feature/panda-cache-adapter-v1 at 1555e3096afbb9c1e177eb6cbc5659341101b4f7. PR112 remains Draft and unmerged.\n\nActual SDK: 996,656 bytes, SHA256 aa7e14e71f98b083faa60536ecf6b0a05e3996b4771d38e4a2ccfd43c0903088; compile/link 144.722615548s. Static data inspection verifies 33 APIs, one source state, original glReadPixels R_X86_64_64 read-tail binding, and rejection by the old ABI profile. Source 7,289 files, private sysroot 665 records, tools and 2,680 SDK outputs are checked. The actual SDK has never been loaded or executed.\n\nValidation:\n\n- 18 focused tests pass (5.849s); full suite: 1,503 tests, 1,496 pass, 7 skipped (122.832s).\n- 102 handwritten CPU shared-library executions (51 normal + 51 ASan/UBSan) have identical scenario results, including default OFF, bootstrap, context, pending lookup and deletion. This CPU library has no actual Panda/GL/X11/ONNX dependency.\n- Missing activity fails a real strict link. Activity-symbol mutation rejects. CI exposed an equivalent internal-linkage spelling of private C++ S; the data inspector now accepts only the two observed spellings while still rejecting separate duplicate storage. The regression reproduced RED then GREEN; failed runs are retained, with no waiver or rerun. Native/build inputs and SDK are unchanged by this inspector fix and were re-audited.\n- Sole whole-branch review: 0 Critical, 1 Important, 0 Minor. The Important ambient RPM_OPT_FLAGS C/C++ header injection was reproduced and fixed by an explicit child-environment allowlist; the actual SDK was rebuilt after that fix. All seven review exclusions have rulings and costs in the ledger; no rereview or minor polishing.\n- 935 indexed proofs / 19,055,272 bytes; 946 additions, zero base-file changes. Earlier before-review and after-fix proof snapshots remain unchanged; ci-fix/ records final verifier/CPU/tests/static data audit.\n\nPreservation checks retain 3,878 base files, 299 previous source pins, 10 original artifacts, main, Draft PRs102\u2013111 and all eight native workflow histories. No main/shared-base update, Cloud/registry publication, consumed request reuse or actual Panda/GL/MetaDrive/provider/official-model/official-ORT execution. Native allowance remains 0; inherited strict result remains 0/4 FAIL and Stage7 INCOMPLETE.\n\nThis qualifies source/build/static linkage only. Compiled branch/alias/name/safe256 coverage, full Python/MetaDrive image parity, mapped origins/new ABI/singleton ownership, actual early install/identity lifetimes, camera/environment, driver/read freshness and authenticated producer/sink/window/process receipts remain unqualified. Next work starts with candidate-specific static coverage; native work requires a fresh bounded contract after the remaining gates.\n\nResults and complete rulings: docs/STAGE7_PANDA_ADAPTER_SDK_RESULT.md, docs/STAGE7_PANDA_ADAPTER_SDK_LEDGER.md, docs/STAGE7_PANDA_ADAPTER_SDK_CONTINUATION.md. Selection/proof index: docs/evidence/panda-adapter-sdk-01/. Final exact-HEAD CI/Draft/body/preservation receipt: output/stage7-panda-adapter-sdk-01/final-verification.json.\n\nExact final-HEAD push and pull_request CI: all four jobs pass.\n\n- pull_request: [43675051251](https://github.com/rownlvh8875-coder/big-model-closed-loop-benchmark/actions/runs/43675051251); synthetic-unit 132693240975, onnx-interface-test 132693241212; both success, attempt 1, artifacts 0.\n- push: [43675047984](https://github.com/rownlvh8875-coder/big-model-closed-loop-benchmark/actions/runs/43675047984); onnx-interface-test 132693231473, synthetic-unit 132693231692; both success, attempt 1, artifacts 0.\n\nThe ONNX interface job uses a generated SMALL TEST GRAPH ONLY; it does not run the official large model. Exact HEAD, attempt/job/artifact checks, Draft/body roundtrip and fresh preservation are retained in the external final receipt. No main/shared-base update or Cloud/registry publication.\n",
